# Code owners — GitHub auto-requests review from these owners when a PR
# touches a matching path.
#
# The main reason this file exists: the schema-sync Action opens a PR whenever
# the upstream BDCHM schema moves (see README, "Keeping the model in sync with
# upstream"). Nothing pushes to main and nothing warns if that PR is ignored —
# the app just keeps serving an older schema. Naming an owner for the schema
# paths means the right person is asked, rather than everyone assuming someone
# else saw it.
#
# WHEN HANDING OFF THIS PROJECT: replace @Sigfried below with whoever becomes
# responsible for updating the model. That is the single edit needed to
# redirect sync notifications.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <owner> [more owners]
# Later matching lines win, so the specific rules below override the catch-all.
# Owners must have write access to the repo or the request is silently dropped.

# Catch-all
*                                   @Sigfried

# Upstream-derived data. These change only via the schema-sync Action.
/public/source_data/                @Sigfried
/scripts/                           @Sigfried

# The sync pipeline itself.
/.github/workflows/schema-sync.yml  @Sigfried

# Ownership classification: hand-curated sets keyed on schema slot names, so an
# upstream rename can change the rendered graph without failing a test.
/src/models/containmentGraph.ts     @Sigfried
/src/config/entityCategories.ts     @Sigfried
/docs/OWNERSHIP_CLASSIFICATION.md   @Sigfried
